From: relay12 contributors
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11on12: receive the sync-token callback result

The same warn_unused_result class as 0010's escape call, at the one other
site GCC named. SyncTokenExtension::Dispatch calls the sync-token callback
through a pointer-to-member and discards the HRESULT.

The discard is deliberate -- the dispatch has already flushed and there is no
path to report a failure from there -- so the result is received and marked
unused rather than handled, which is what a (void) cast fails to do for a
function carrying the attribute.

Two neighbouring callback calls, pfnSetErrorCb and
pfnPerformAmortizedProcessingCb in device.cpp, also discard their results and
are deliberately left alone: GCC named only this one, so only this one
carries the attribute.
---
diff --git a/src/present.cpp b/src/present.cpp
index 480e933..2219056 100644
--- a/src/present.cpp
+++ b/src/present.cpp
@@ -55,7 +55,14 @@ namespace D3D11On12
         SyncTokenExtensionData data = *reinterpret_cast<SyncTokenExtensionData const*>(pData);
         D3DDDICB_SYNCTOKEN SyncTokenCB = {};
         SyncTokenCB.hSyncToken = data.hSyncToken;
-        (m_Device->m_pKTCallbacks->*m_pCallback)(m_Device->m_hRTDevice.handle, &SyncTokenCB);
+        // Best-effort, as in Device::ReportError: the dispatch has
+        // already flushed and there is no path to report a failure
+        // from here. A (void) cast does not satisfy
+        // warn_unused_result, so receive the value and drop it.
+        const HRESULT syncTokenStatus =
+                (m_Device->m_pKTCallbacks->*m_pCallback)(
+                        m_Device->m_hRTDevice.handle, &SyncTokenCB);
+        (void)syncTokenStatus;
         if (data.sharingContractPresentResource)
         {
             m_Device->GetImmediateContextNoFlush().SharingContractPresent(data.sharingContractPresentResource->ImmediateResource());
